   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Keno has its roots in China, and Chinese immigrants brought it to America in the late eighteen hundreds.",
   "cap": "Keno has its roots in China,|and Chinese immigrants|brought it to America|in the late 1800s.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "The ticket has eighty numbers, and you mark anywhere from one to twenty of them.",
   "cap": "The ticket has 80 numbers,|and you mark anywhere|from 1 to 20 of them.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Then twenty numbers are drawn, and you are paid by how many of yours match.",
   "cap": "Then 20 numbers are drawn,|and you are paid|by how many of yours match.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "There is no strategy at all, because every number is as likely as any other.",
   "cap": "There is no strategy at all,|because every number|is as likely as any other.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Mark just four numbers, and all four come up about once in three hundred twenty six games.",
   "cap": "Mark just four numbers,|and all four come up|about once in 326 games.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Here is the catch. On one sample four number pay table, a dollar returns about eighty cents.",
   "cap": "Here is the catch.|On one sample|four number pay table,|a dollar returns|about 80 cents.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Keno pays back anywhere from under seventy to just over eighty percent. The house keeps the rest.",
   "cap": "Keno pays back anywhere|from under 70|to just over 80%.|The house keeps the rest.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "And all ten out of ten? About one in eight point nine million.",
   "cap": "And all ten out of ten?|About 1 in 8.9 million.",
   "pause": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "There are no lucky numbers in keno. There is only the house edge.",
   "cap": "There are no lucky numbers|in keno. There is only|the house edge.",
   "pause": 0.45
  }
